<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="CRT.SystemDeletionView">

    <!--
    DELETE A SYSTEM (owner request, 2026-10-03: "as admin, I should be able to have a possibility to
    delete a system completely, which then will remove it from everywhere - including BETA and
    stable sources ... part of the 'Admin' menu, that only I do have access to, and then just list
    all systems and have a delete button on each (with a confirmation box)"). ADMINISTRATOR ONLY,
    like every padlocked entry on the Account screen (the Admin screen until 2026-10-04) - the server refuses everybody else regardless.

    Every system the Systems screen lists, each with its grey line (where its data is, who maintains
    it) and a red Delete button. Delete asks the server what would go and shows that in
    DeleteSystemWindow; nothing is deleted before the confirmation. A system that cannot be deleted
    says why here, in the server's words, and no confirmation opens.

    The rows sit in a ScrollViewer: a system list is tens of rows, not the thousands a file tree has.
    -->
    <DockPanel>

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   x:Name="HeadingText"
                   FontWeight="SemiBold"
                   FontSize="14"
                   Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   x:Name="ExplanationText"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   Opacity="0.8"
                   Margin="0,0,0,12" />

        <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Top"
                   x:Name="MessageText"
                   TextWrapping="Wrap"
                   IsVisible="False"
                   Margin="0,0,0,8" />

        <ScrollViewer HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
            <StackPanel x:Name="SystemsPanel" Margin="0,0,12,0" />
        </ScrollViewer>
    </DockPanel>
</UserControl>
